       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, and I shouldn't have offered it as an option in my last message. 7,650 mg/day of metformin is three times the maximum labeled dose. It has no added glycemic benefit, and it carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis even with normal renal function. I can't think of a clinical scenario where it would be appropriate, so I don't want to put it into the system.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum dose.\n- **Metformin 500 mg PO BID with meals**, or another starting or titration dose you choose.\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO BID with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nIf you have an unusual situation that I'm missing, you could talk to pharmacy. They can review it and help place an override through the proper channel."
